class Solution {
    public boolean isAdjacentDiffAtMostTwo(String s) {
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length() - 1; i++) {
            // Calculate the absolute difference between two adjacent characters
            int diff = Math.abs(s.charAt(i) - s.charAt(i + 1));
            if (diff > 2) { // If the difference is greater than 2, condition fails → return false
                return false;
            }
        }
        // If all adjacent differences are ≤ 2, return true
        return true;
    }
}

Time Complexity: 
𝑂(𝑛) — proportional to the number of characters in the string.

Space Complexity: 
𝑂(1) — uses constant memory regardless of input size.
